# fastly_ngwaf_workspace_templated_signal_rule (Resource)

Manages a Fastly Next-Gen WAF `templated_signal` rule scoped to a single
workspace: it adds one of Fastly's templated signals to matching requests.

Two things set this rule type apart from the others:

- It takes no `description`; the API accepts only an empty one.
- Every change replaces the rule. The API rejects an update to a
  `templated_signal` rule that carries actions, and its action is mandatory,
  so there is nothing to change in place.

Rules of other types are managed by their own resources -
`fastly_ngwaf_workspace_request_rule`,
`fastly_ngwaf_workspace_signal_rule`, and
`fastly_ngwaf_workspace_rate_limit_rule`. All four can be read back together
via the `fastly_ngwaf_workspace_rules` data source.

## Example Usage

```terraform
resource "fastly_ngwaf_workspace" "example" {
  name        = "Example Workspace"
  description = "Managed by Terraform"
  mode        = "block"

  attack_signal_thresholds {}
}

resource "fastly_ngwaf_workspace_templated_signal_rule" "login_attempt_signal" {
  workspace_id = fastly_ngwaf_workspace.example.id
  enabled      = true

  condition {
    field    = "path"
    operator = "equals"
    value    = "/login"
  }

  action {
    signal = "LOGINATTEMPT"
  }
}
```

{{ .SchemaMarkdown | trimspace }}

## Import

Next-Gen WAF workspace templated signal rules are imported using a
combination of the workspace ID and the rule ID, separated by a `/`:

```shell
terraform import fastly_ngwaf_workspace_templated_signal_rule.example WORKSPACE_ID/RULE_ID
```
